If the app hangs after the first frame once Mesa's software OpenGL fallback
activates, that's a known issue with Mesa's fast "llvmpipe" rasterizer on some
VMs with a conservative default virtual CPU model (e.g. Proxmox's kvm64 or
qemu64). To force the slower but unconditionally stable "softpipe" rasterizer
instead, rename this file to ".force-mesa-compat" — remove the ".sample"
extension. Only the file's name and location matter; this text is never read
by the app. Force-quit the hung app first (Task Manager), then relaunch after
renaming this file.
